    "created_at": "2021-11-30T05:31:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-30T05:31:32Z",
    "body": "> Looks reasonable so far. Should we make unbuffered transforms the default? I suspect it's more desirable, and hopefully wouldn't be too breaking...\r\n\r\nI'm concerned that people may be relying on the existing behaviour. With buffering, all the transforms in a pipe can run in parallel, but without it they will run in series. This could cause mysterious performance regressions.",
